From: robertijtsma <37256770+robertijtsma@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: venus: port SQ2 Iris1 HFI4 decoder backend to Linux 7.3

Ports the SC8180X / Surface Pro X SQ2 Iris1 HFI4 hardware video decoder
backend (originating from lhf1a/googlebookos_surface_pro_x) to Linux 7.3:

- Adds explicit opt-in platform match ("microsoft,sq2-venus-lab", guarded
  by module parameter sq2_platform_allow=1) with dedicated power/clock/
  reset/ICC ownership, PIL gap firmware loading at 0x8c000000 via EL1
  TrustZone SCM PAS 9, and HFI4 Windows-reference queue/SMMU layout.
- Accepts both Surface Pro X SQ2 venus.mbn releases
  (VIDEO.IR.1.2-00042-PROD-1 and VIDEO.IR.1.2-00079-PROD-2) and allows
  merged UEFI reserved /proc/iomem parent ranges (>= PIL end).
- Adapts upstream Linux 7.3 Venus changes (void venus_remove(),
  hfi_bufreq_get_count_min(), kzalloc_obj(), MODULE_IMPORT_NS("DMA_BUF"),
  upstream P010 format support, and venus_close_common() teardown ordering
  in vdec_close() so v4l2_m2m_ctx_release() runs vdec_session_release()
  before the SQ2 SESSION_END close guard).

Verified on live SQ2 hardware (7.3.1-1-surface) with bit-exact SHA-256
matches against FFmpeg software decoding across 4K H.264 (3840x2160),
4K HEVC (3840x2160), and 1080p VP9 (1920x1080) over repeated sessions.
